# Vial size and label profile

Discuss and reason about **vial size** (e.g. **3 ml**, **10 ml**) as the product concept; **label dimensions and preview scaling** follow from the active **print target**.

## Vial profiles (product intent)

Implemented and planned vial sizes are described in [docs/FRD.md](../../docs/FRD.md) (**Today** / **Planned**). **3 ml** is wired in print setup as a soft recommendation; **10 ml** is planned.

| Vial size | Code source of truth | Notes |
|-----------|----------------------|--------|
| **3 ml** | `src/features/label/print/` (`printCatalog.ts` recommendations) | Default skip target **40 × 20 mm rounded @ 300 DPI**; vial soft-ranks stock suggestions. |
| **10 ml** | Not implemented | See FRD **Planned**; add catalog recommendation rows when built. |

When the user has not named a vial size, follow **`label-work-clarify-vial-size.mdc`** before changing label-related behavior.

## Mental model

- **`src/features/label/print/`** is canonical for mm, DPI, export pixels, catalog, and filtering. **`dimensions.ts`** is the only mm→px conversion.
- **`PrintTarget`** flows through layout (`LabelLayoutEngine`), preview (`Scaling`, `LabelPreview`), and export (`buildExportSpec`, `LabelStage`).
- Skip default: **40 × 20 mm rounded @ 300 DPI**; **label stock** (shape + per-stock padding) drives preview layout. **Printer selection** sets export DPI when chosen (e.g. B21 @ 203, M2 @ 300).
- PNG/export constraints: **`thermal-print-output.mdc`**.

Prefer checking **export/preview at realistic zoom** for the **active print target**, not full-screen dev chrome.
